{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"pages":{"2481":{"pageid":2481,"ns":0,"title":"Block","revisions":[{"revid":56030,"parentid":56029,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Keyword Infobox\n |Name        = Block\n |Image       = Icon Block.png\n |Description = Until next turn, prevents damage.\n}}\n{{KW|Block}} is the amount of damage a character or enemy can take before they lose HP.\n\nBy default, {{KW|Block}} is removed at the end of each turn.\n\n{{BD|Dexterity}} and {{BD|Frail}} modifies the {{KW|Block}} you gain from playing non-power cards. However, it does not apply to cards that depend on other effects to generate {{KW|Block}}, like {{C|Rage}} or {{C|Wallop}}.\n\n== Sources ==\n=== On Player ===\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Defend (Ironclad)|Defend}}: Gain 5 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">8</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Armaments}}: Gain 5 {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Iron Wave}}: Gain 5 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">7</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Shrug It Off}}: Gain 8 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">11</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|True Grit}}: Gain 7 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">9</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Entrench}}: Double your {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Feel No Pain}}: Gain 3 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">4</span>) {{BD|Feel No Pain|Block}} whenever you {{KW|Exhaust}} a card.\n* {{C|Flame Barrier}}: Gain 12 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">16</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Ghostly Armor}}: Gain 10 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">13</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Metallicize}}: Gain 3 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">4</span>) {{BD|Metallicize|Block}} at the end of each turn.\n* {{C|Power Through}}: Gain 15 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">20</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Rage}}: Gain 3 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">5</span>) {{BD|Rage|Block}} whenever you play an Attack this turn.\n* {{C|Second Wind}}: {{KW|Exhaust}} all non-Attack cards in hand. Gain 5 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">7</span>) {{KW|Block}} for each card {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}.\n* {{C|Sentinel}}: Gain 5 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">8</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Impervious}}: Gain 30 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">40</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Survivor}}: Gain 8 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">11</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Backflip}}: Gain 5 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">8</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Cloak and Dagger}}: Gain 6 {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Deflect}}: Gain 4 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">7</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Dodge and Roll}}: Gain 4 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">6</span>) {{KW|Block}}. Next turn, gain 4 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">6</span>) {{BD|Next Turn Block|Block}}.\n* {{C|Blur}}: Gain 5 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">8</span>) {{KW|Block}}. {{BD|Blur|Block}} is not removed at the start of next turn.\n* {{C|Dash}}: Gain 10 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">13</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Escape Plan}}: Gain 3 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">5</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Leg Sweep}}: Gain 11 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">14</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|After Image}}: Gain 1 {{BD|After Image|Block}} whenever you play a card.\n* {{C|Charge Battery}}: Gain 7 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">10</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Cold Snap}}: {{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Frost}}.\n* {{C|Coolheaded}}: {{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Frost}}.\n* {{C|Hologram}}: Gain 3 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">5</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Leap}}: Gain 9 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">12</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Stack}}: Gain {{KW|Block}} equal to the number of cards in your discard pile (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">plus 3</span>).\n* {{C|Steam Barrier}}: Gain 6 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">8</span>) {{KW|Block}}. Decrease this card's {{KW|Block}} by 1 this combat.\n* {{C|Auto-Shields}}: If you have no {{KW|Block}}, gain 11 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">15</span>).\n* {{C|Boot Sequence}}: Gain 10 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">13</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Chaos}}: You may {{KW|Channel}} up to 1 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">2</span>) {{KW|Frost}}.\n* {{C|Chill}}: {{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Frost}} for each enemy in combat.\n* {{C|Equilibrium}}: Gain 13 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">16</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Force Field}}: Gain 12 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">16</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Genetic Algorithm}}: Gain 1 {{KW|Block}}. Permanently increses this card's {{KW|Block}} by 2 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">3</span>).\n* {{C|Glacier}}: Gain 7 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">10</span>) {{KW|Block}}. {{KW|Channel}} 2 {{KW|Frost}}.\n* {{C|Reinforced Body}}: Gain 7 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">9</span>) {{KW|Block}} X times.\n* {{C|Rainbow}}: {{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Frost}}.\n* {{C|Vigilance}}: Gain 8 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">12</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Empty Body}}: Gain 7 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">10</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Evaluate}}: Gain 6 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">10</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Halt}}: Gain 3 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">4</span>) {{KW|Block}}. If you are in {{KW|Wrath}}, gain 9 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">14</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Just Lucky}}: Gain 2 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">3</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Prostrate}}: Gain 4 {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Protect}}: Gain 12 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">16</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Third Eye}}: Gain 7 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">9</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Deceive Reality}}: Gain 4 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">7</span>) {{KW|Block}}. Add a {{C|Safety}} to your hand.\n* {{C|Like Water}}: Gain 5 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">7</span>) {{BD|Like Water|Block}} whenever you end your turn in {{KW|Calm}}.\n* {{C|Mental Fortress}}: Gain 4 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">6</span>) {{BD|Mental Fortress|Block}} whenever you change {{KW|Stance|Stances}}.\n* {{C|Nirvana}}: Gain 3 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">4</span>) {{BD|Nirvana|Block}} whenever you {{KW|Scry}}.\n* {{C|Perseverance}}: Gain 5 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">7</span>) {{KW|Block}}. When {{KW|Retain|Retained}}, increase this card's {{KW|Block}} by 2 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">3</span>) this combat.\n* {{C|Sanctity}}: Gain 6 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">9</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Swivel}}: Gain 8 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">11</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Talk to the Hand}}: Whenever you attack target enemy, gain 2 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">3</span>) {{BD|Block Return|Block}}.\n* {{C|Wallop}}: Deal 9 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">12</span>) damage. Gain {{KW|Block}} equal to unblocked damage dealt.\n* {{C|Spirit Shield}}: Gain 3 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">4</span>) {{KW|Block}} for each card in hand.\n* {{C|Wish}}: Gain 6 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">8</span>) {{BD|Plated Armor}}.\n* {{C|Finesse}}: Gain 2 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">4</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Good Instincts}}: Gain 6 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">9</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Panic Button}}: Gain 30 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">40</span>) {{KW|Block}}. You cannot gain {{BD|No Block|Block}} from cards for 2 turns.\n* {{C|Safety}}: Gain 12 (<span class=\"stat-upgraded\">16</span>) {{KW|Block}}.\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Anchor}}: Start combat with 10 {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{R|Orichalcum}}: Whenever you end turn without {{KW|Block}}, gain 6.\n* {{R|Horn Cleat}}: Gain 14 {{KW|Block}} at the start of your second turn.\n* {{R|Ornamental Fan}}: Gain 4 {{KW|Block}} whenever you play 3 Attacks in a turn.\n* {{R|Self-Forming Clay}}: Whenever you lose HP, gain 3 {{BD|Next Turn Block|Block}} next turn.\n* {{R|Captain's Wheel}}: Gain 18 {{KW|Block}} at the start of your third turn.\n* {{R|Cloak Clasp}}: Gain 1 {{KW|Block}} for each card you have in hand at the end of your turn.\n* {{R|Thread and Needle}}: Start combat with 4 {{BD|Plated Armor}}.\n* {{R|Tough Bandages}}: Gain 3 {{KW|Block}} whenever you [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] a card.\n* {{R|The Abacus}}: Gain 6 {{KW|Block}} whenever you shuffle your discard pile into your draw pile.\n* {{R|Frozen Core}}: {{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Frost}} whenever you end your turn with an empty [[Orbs#Orb_Slot|Orb Slot]].\n\n==== Potions ====\n* {{P|Block Potion}}: Gain 12 ({{R|Sacred Bark|24}}) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{P|Essence of Steel}}: Gain 4 ({{R|Sacred Bark|8}}) {{BD|Plated Armor}}.\n* {{P|Heart of Iron}}: Gain 6 ({{R|Sacred Bark|12}}) {{BD|Metallicize|Block}} at the end of each turn.\n\n=== On Enemies ===\n----\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Melter}}: Enemy <span class=\"negative-text\">loses</span> all {{KW|Block}}.\n\n==== Monsters ====\n* {{M|Jaw Worm}}\n** In [[Act 3]], starts combat with 6 ({{Asc|17|9}}) {{KW|Block}}.\n** {{Int|Jaw Worm|Thrash}}: Gain 5 {{KW|Block}}.\n** {{Int|Jaw Worm|Bellow}}: Gain 6 ({{Asc|17|9}}) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{M|Red Louse}}, {{M|Green Louse}}\n** Starts combat with 3-7 ({{Asc|7|4-8}}, {{Asc|17|9-12}}) {{BD|Curl Up}}.\n* {{M|Shield Gremlin}}\n** {{Int|Shield Gremlin|Protect}}: Target enemy gains 7 ({{Asc|2|8}}, {{Asc|17|11}}) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{M|Looter}}\n** {{Int|Looter|Smoke Bomb}}: Gain 6 {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{M|Mugger}}\n** {{Int|Mugger|Smoke Bomb}}: Gain 11 ({{Asc|17|17}}) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{M|Shelled Parasite}}\n** Starts combat with 14 {{BD|Plated Armor}}.\n* {{M|Spheric Guardian}}\n** Starts combat with 40 {{KW|Block}} and {{BD|Barricade}}.\n** {{Int|Spheric Guardian|Activate}}: Gain 25 ({{Asc|17|35}}) {{KW|Block}}.\n** {{Int|Spheric Guardian|Harden}}: Gain 15 {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{M|Centurion}}\n** {{Int|Centurion|Protect}}: Target enemy gains 15 ({{Asc|17|20}}) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{M|Snake Plant}}\n** Starts combat with 3 {{BD|Malleable}}.\n* {{M|Bear}}\n** {{Int|Bear|Lunge}}: Gain 9 {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{M|Darkling}}\n** {{Int|Darkling|Harden}}: Gain 12 {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{M|Writhing Mass}}\n** Starts combat with 3 {{BD|Malleable}}.\n** {{Int|Writhing Mass|Block Attack}}: Gain 16 ({{Asc|2|18}}) {{KW|Block}}.\n\n==== Elites ====\n* The [[Elites#Super_Elites|Super Elite]] may start combat with 4/6/8 {{BD|Metallicize}} in [[Acts|Act]] 1/2/3.\n* {{M|Lagavulin}}\n** Starts combat with 8 {{BD|Metallicize}}. Loses when waking up.\n* {{M|Gremlin Leader}}\n** {{Int|Gremlin Leader|Encourage}}: All minions gain 6 ({{Asc|18|10}}) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{M|Spire Shield}}\n** {{Int|Spire Shield|Fortify}}: All enemies gain 30 {{KW|Block}}.\n** {{Int|Spire Shield|Smash}}: Deal 34 damage and gain that much {{KW|Block}}. On [[Ascension|Ascension 18+]], instead gain 99 {{KW|Block}}.\n\n==== Bosses ====\n* {{M|The Guardian}}\n** Starts combat with {{BD|Mode Shift}}: After losing 30 ({{Asc|9|35}}, {{Asc|19|40}}) HP, gains 20 {{KW|Block}}.\n** {{Int|The Guardian|Charging Up}}: Gain 9 {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{M|Hexaghost}}\n** {{Int|Hexaghost|Inflame}}: Gain 12 {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{M|Bronze Automaton}}\n** {{Int|Bronze Automaton|Boost}}: Gain 9 ({{Asc|9|12}}) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{M|Bronze Orb}}\n** {{Int|Bronze Orb|Support Beam}}: {{M|Bronze Automaton}} gains 12 {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{M|The Champ}}\n** {{Int|The Champ|Defensive Stance}}: Gain 15 ({{Asc|9|18}}, {{Asc|19|20}}) {{KW|Block}}. Gain 5 ({{Asc|9|6}}, {{Asc|19|7}}) {{BD|Metallicize|Block}} at the end of each turn.\n* {{M|The Collector}}\n** {{Int|The Collector|Buff}}: Gain 15 ({{Asc|9|18}}, {{Asc|19|23}}) {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{M|Deca}}\n** {{Int|Deca|Square of Protection}}: All enemies gain 16 {{KW|Block}} and {{Asc|19|3}} {{BD|Plated Armor}}.\n* {{M|Time Eater}}\n** {{Int|Time Eater|Ripple}}: Gain 20 {{KW|Block}}.\n** {{Int|Time Eater|Haste}}: Gain {{Asc|19|32}} {{KW|Block}}.\n\n==== Other ====\n* {{R|Ancient Augmentation}}: Enemies start combat with 10 {{BD|Plated Armor}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n* Other than sources of {{BD|Dexterity}} and {{BD|Frail}}, the following things interact with {{KW|Block}}: {{C|Body Slam}}, {{C|Entrench}}, {{C|Barricade}}, {{C|Juggernaut}}, {{C|Blur}}, {{C|Melter}}, {{C|Wave of the Hand}}, {{C|Panic Button}}, {{R|Calipers}} and {{R|Hand Drill}}.\n\n* And these things interact with ''unblocked'' damage: {{C|Rupture}}, {{C|Reaper}}, {{C|Envenom}}, {{C|Static Discharge}}, {{C|Wallop}}, {{R|The Boot}}, {{R|Torii}}, {{R|Tungsten Rod}}, {{BD|Plated Armor}}, {{BD|Malleable}}, {{BD|Painful Stabs}} and {{BD|Reactive}}.\n\n* Cards that directly remove HP ignore {{KW|Block}}.\n** On the Player, they are {{C|Bloodletting}}, {{C|Combust}}, {{C|Hemokinesis}}, {{C|Brutality}} {{C|Offering}}, {{C|J.A.X.}}, {{C|Pain}}, {{C|Regret}} and any Curse played with {{R|Blue Candle}}.\n** On enemies, they are {{C|Choke}}, {{C|Pressure Points}}, {{C|Judgment}} and any source of {{BD|Poison}}.\n** {{C|Melter}} does not remove HP, but in practice it also ignores {{KW|Block}}.\n\n* {{BD|Dexterity}}, {{BD|Frail}} and {{BD|No Block}} do not work with [[Relics]], [[Potions]] or [[Orbs]].\n** They also ignore the following cards: {{C|Entrench}}, {{C|Feel No Pain}}, {{C|Metallicize}}, {{C|Rage}}, {{C|After Image}}, {{C|Like Water}}, {{C|Mental Fortress}}, {{C|Nirvana}}, {{C|Talk to the Hand}}, {{C|Wallop}} and {{C|Wish}}.\n\n* Maximum {{KW|Block}} is 999.\n\n{{Clear}}\n<!--\n== Hints ==\n-->\n== Achievements ==\n=== BARRICADED ===\n* Unlocks when {{KW|Block}} reaches '''999''' combat.\n\n=== IMPERVIOUS ===\n* Unlocks when {{KW|Block}} reaches '''99''' or more during combat.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Fixed damage and block values showing green increased values when the end value was the same.\n** Fixed Invincible power with interactions such as The Boot and Block.\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** Keywords are now always gold in descriptions. Block, Vulnerable, etc.\n* '''Weekly Patch 41: Chill'''\n** Fixed bug causing block to maintain between colosseum combats.\n* '''Weekly Patch 20: Immolate'''\n** Edge case fixes for incorrect Block rounding with multiple powers.\n* '''Weekly Patch 18: Paranormal'''\n** Fix for Block calculation with multiple modifiers incorrectly rounding.\n* '''Weekly Patch 17: Patched in the Face'''\n** Exploder's explosion no longer ignores block.\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Block and Deck count are now in a bolder font.\n* '''Day 1 Patch'''\n** Adding logic to prevent scale cannot be 0 issue for Blocked Number VFX.\n\n[[Category:Game Mechanics]]"}}}]},"2067":{"pageid":2067,"ns":0,"title":"Dark","revisions":[{"revid":56039,"parentid":55722,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Keyword Infobox\n |Name        = Dark\n |Image       = DarkOrb.png\n |Description = '''Passive''': Increase stored damage by 6 (+1 per {{BD|Focus}}).<br>{{KW|Evoke}}: Deal stored damage damage to the enemy with the least HP.\n}}\n{{KW|Dark|Dark Orbs}} are the less common type of damage dealing [[Orb]], with an emphasis on scaling. Dark Orbs have a damage value, which starts at 6 when {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}, and their [[Orbs#Passive|Passive]] adds (6 + {{BD|Focus}}) to the damage value at end of turn. When {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}}, the Orbs deal their current damage value to the enemy with the lowest current HP, in contrast to {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orb's}} random targeting.\n\nDark Orbs are much less common than {{KW|Lightning}} and {{KW|Frost}} Orbs, and generally require a different approach. While the other Orb types have similar effects for their Passive and Evoked abilities, Dark Orbs do very little if Evoked before applying their Passive, and benefit from their Passive ability being used before Evoking.\n\n== Dark Sources ==\n=== Cards ===\n* {{C|Darkness}}\n* {{C|Doom and Gloom}}\n* {{C|Chaos}}\n* {{C|Rainbow}}\n\n=== Relic ===\n* {{R|Symbiotic Virus}}\n\n=== Potion ===\n* {{P|Essence of Darkness}}\n\n== Interactions ==\n* Dark damage bypasses anything that effects {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards, like {{BD|Flying}}, {{BD|Thorns}}, and {{BD|Slow}}.\n* Dark Orbs always target the lowest HP enemy when Evoked, which can cause small enemies like {{BD|Minion|Minions}} to take the damage before larger ones. However, multi-Evoking a Dark Orb with cards like {{C|Dualcast}} and {{C|Multi-Cast}} will retarget each instance of damage, possibly clearing out small enemies and hitting the large one all in one go.\n\n== Synergies ==\n\n* Dark Orbs particularly benefit from effects that cause extra [[Orbs#Passive|Passives]], allowing them to scale up faster.\n** {{C|Loop}} and {{R|Gold-Plated Cables}} each cause your right most Orb to get an extra Passive each turn (2 extra if Loop is upgraded).\n** {{R|Emotion Chip}} gives all your Orbs up to one additional Passive each turn, if you lost HP the previous turn.\n** {{C|Darkness|Darkness+}} will give all of your Dark Orbs an extra Passive when played, in addition to Channeling a Dark Orb.\n* In addition, as individual Dark Orbs can have quite substantial effect when {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}}, benefitting from cards which Evoke them repeatedly:\n** {{C|Dualcast}} and {{C|Multi-Cast}} can {{KW|Evoke}} a Dark Orb 2 or X times, respectively. As [[The Defect]] can generate quite a lot of {{Icon|BE}} Energy in one turn, {{C|Multi-Cast}} in particular can be a potent finisher for Dark Orbs.\n** While {{C|Recursion}} only {{KW|Evoke|Evokes}} an Orb once, it also moves it to the back of your Orb Slots. This allows you to Evoke that Dark Orb again later, as well as giving it more time to grow first.\n* {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, and {{C|Biased Cognition}} all provide {{BD|Focus}}, which increases the rate at which Dark Orbs scale up.\n** Notably, the base damage of Dark Orbs is ''not'' affected by {{BD|Focus}}, and they will always start at 6 damage when {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n\n* {{C|Bullseye}} applies {{BD|Lock-On}}, which makes damaging Orbs deal 50% more damage to that enemy.\n* {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, and {{P|Potion of Capacity}} all increase your number of Orb Slots, allowing more Orb Passives in parallel.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb.\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws an additional card for each type of unique Orb Channeled.\n* {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb. However, unless it is upgraded, the Orbs will simply be removed, wasting any Dark Orbs that were Channeled.\n\n== Anti-Synergies ==\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making Dark Orbs scale slower.\n** However, as this only affects the future growth of Dark Orbs, the downside is minimized later into fights, once your Orbs have had to time to scale up already. As such, {{C|Hyperbeam}} may work to clear small enemies before {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} your Dark Orbs.\n* {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Powers}} which cause you to {{KW|Channel}} Orbs automatically such as {{C|Static Discharge}} and {{C|Storm}} can make it difficult to hold Dark Orbs until the correct moment.\n\n[[Category:Orbs]]"}}}]},"1901":{"pageid":1901,"ns":0,"title":"Exhaust","revisions":[{"revid":56164,"parentid":56163,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Keyword Infobox\n |Name = Exhaust\n |Description = Removed until the end of combat.\n}}\n{{KW|Exhaust}} is a [[Keywords|Keyword]] that appears on cards. When a card with '''Exhaust''' is played it is moved to the exhaust pile until the end of combat.\n\n== Sources and Interactions ==\n{{SortedQuery/all\n| Keyword = Exhaust\n| Header = h3\n| SubHeader = h4\n}}\n\n[[Category:Game Mechanics]] [[Category:toUpdate]]"}}}]},"2068":{"pageid":2068,"ns":0,"title":"Frost","revisions":[{"revid":55794,"parentid":54200,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Keyword Infobox\n |Name        = Frost\n |Image       = FrostOrb.png\n |Description = '''Passive''': Gain 2 (+1 per {{BD|Focus}}) {{KW|Block}}.<br>{{KW|Evoke}}: Gain 5 (+1 per {{BD|Focus}}) {{KW|Block}}.\n}}\n{{KW|Frost|Frost Orbs}} are the {{KW|Block}} generating [[Orbs]]. Their [[Orbs#Passive|Passive]] effect gives (2 + {{BD|Focus}}) {{KW|Block}} at end of turn, while the {{KW|Evoke}} effect gives (5 + {{BD|Focus}}) {{KW|Block}}.\n\nFrost is the second most common Orb type, being generated by nearly as many sources as {{KW|Lightning}}.\n\n== Frost Sources ==\n=== Cards ===\n* {{C|Cold Snap}}\n* {{C|Coolheaded}}\n* {{C|Chill}}\n* {{C|Chaos}}\n* {{C|Glacier}}\n* {{C|Rainbow}}\n\n=== Relic ===\n* {{R|Frozen Core}}\n\n== Interactions ==\n* Frost Orbs are not affected by {{BD|Dexterity}} and {{BD|Frail}}.\n* {{R|Orichalcum}} will apply {{KW|Block}} even if Frost Orbs are going off at the same time, allowing the two to stack.\n* If a Frost Orb is {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} during the Enemy turn, such as due to {{C|Static Discharge}}, the {{KW|Block}} will be applied immediately, possibly decreasing further incoming damage.\n* {{KW|Block}} from Frost Orbs is added before the damage from {{C|Decay}} and {{C|Burn}} is applied.\n\n== Synergies ==\n* {{C|Blizzard}} deals more damage for each Frost Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat.\n* {{C|Loop}}, {{R|Gold-Plated Cables}}, and {{R|Emotion Chip}} can each trigger additional Frost Orb passives per turn, providing additional {{KW|Block}}.\n** Of these, {{C|Loop}} and {{R|Emotion Chip}} both do so at the beginning of your turn, which is particularly useful agains {{BD|Thorns}} and {{BD|Beat of Death}}.\n\n* {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, and {{P|Potion of Capacity}} all increase your number of Orb Slots, allowing more Orb Passives in parallel.\n* {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, and {{C|Biased Cognition}} all provide {{BD|Focus}}, which increases the {{KW|Block}} provided by Frost Orbs.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n** {{C|Fission|Fission+}} also {{KW|Evoke|Evokes}} all of the Orbs, allowing a huge amount of {{KW|Block}} from Frost Orbs in a single turn.\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws an additional card for each type of unique Orb Channeled.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Frost Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n* As Frost Orbs provide {{KW|Block}} without playing a card, they bypass the downside of {{C|Panic Button}}.\n\n== Anti-Synergies ==\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making Frost Orbs less effective.\n\n[[Category:Orbs]]"}}}]},"1747":{"pageid":1747,"ns":0,"title":"Keywords","revisions":[{"revid":55679,"parentid":45695,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Ambox\n| title = WARNING!\n| color = red\n| icon = GremlinNob.png\n| message = ''This page is under construction. Information may be wrong or incomplete.''\n}}\n{{TOC limit|3}}\n\n== Common to all characters ==\n=== Block ===\n{{Hatnote|See [[Block]] for more info on its sources and interactions.}}\n{{KW|Block}} is a resource used by all characters as well as a number of enemies to reduce damage taken in a turn. Block is removed at the start of your turn unless you are under the effects of {{C|Barricade}} or {{C|Blur}}. The {{R|Calipers}} Relic also mitigates the end-of-turn loss of Block.\n\n'''Example:''' Player takes 20 damage while having 8 {{KW|Block}} so the total damage taken will be 20 - 8 or 12.\n\n=== Energy ===\nEnergy is a resource used to play cards. Every character gains 3 Energy at the start of their turn. Energy can be gained through other [[Cards]] or [[Relics]].\n\nEvery character's cards have their own symbol for Energy. \n\n{{Icon|RE}} for Ironclad\n\n{{Icon|GE}} for Silent\n\n{{Icon|BE}} for Defect\n\n{{Icon|PE}} for Watcher\n\n{{Icon|CE}} for all {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless Cards}}\n\n== Card Modifiers ==\n=== Exhaust ===\nExhausting a card removes it from play for the rest of combat and places it in the Exhaust pile which can be viewed during combat. Most cards Exhaust themselves on use, however some cards can Exhaust others.\n\nThe only way to get an Exhausted card back is using the [[Ironclad]] card {{C|Exhume}} which will bring back one card and then Exhaust itself.\n\n=== Ethereal ===\nEthereal cards are automatically Exhausted if they are in your hand at the end of your turn.\n\n[[Curse|Curses]] and [[Status|Statuses]] trigger before exhaust.\n\n=== Innate ===\nInnate is a card modifier that makes that card appear in the first hand of cards you draw during combat. This is not in addition to the default card draw at the start of a turn; an Innate card will take up one of those slots. However, if the number of Innate cards in your deck exceeds the number of cards you draw in your first hand, all the Innate cards will still be drawn, effectively functioning as free card draw.\n\nIn some cases it may be beneficial to avoid some Innate cards because they can take up the draw slots of potentially more beneficial cards.\n\nThe {{R|Bottled Flame}}, {{R|Bottled Lightning}}, and {{R|Bottled Tornado}} Relics have an effect similar to Innate but are different in a few key ways. First of all, when duplicating a bottled card, the other copy will not appear in your hand at the start of combat. Bottled cards cannot be removed from your deck but can be transformed, which will not put the new card in place of the old one. The bottle relic will still say \"Start each combat with [name of previous card] in your hand\" this is a visual bug and the relic will now have no effect.\n\n=== Unplayable ===\nMost {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}} as well as a few {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Statuses}} are unable to be played from your hand. One of the only examples of an unplayable card that is beneficial is {{C|Tactician}}, which cannot be played but can be discarded in order to gain {{Icon|GE}} Energy.\n* {{R|Medical Kit}} and {{R|Blue Candle}} are the only [[relics]] that allow you to use Unplayble cards.\n\n=== Retain ===\nRetain is a card modifier only found on some {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher Cards}}. Cards with Retain on them will not be discarded at the end of your turn and will persist until played or removed by other means such as {{KW|Exhaust}}. Some {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}} will still be discarded at the end of your turn even if Retained.\n\nThe effects of {{R|Runic Pyramid}} are similar to Retain, but not strictly speaking the same thing. As such, {{C|Establishment}} will not interact with this relic.\n\n== Character Specific ==\n=== Discard ===\nWhile not a defined Keyword in the game, '''Discard''' is a mostly [[Silent]] exclusive mechanic. Cards can be discarded from your hand into your '''Discard Pile''', in exchange for a buff or to simply cycle them out of your hand. [[Defect]] is the only other character with access to '''Discard''', with the card {{C|Scrape}}. \n\n'''Discarding''' your hand at the end of your turn does not trigger '''Discard''' mechanics.\n\nWatcher's [[#Scry|Scry]] does not trigger '''Discard''' mechanics, and only functions as deck cycling.\n\n==== Sources ====\nThese are the all the sources of Discard in the game:\n\n===== Cards =====\n{{C|Survivor}}, {{C|Prepared}}, {{C|Acrobatics}}, {{C|Dagger Throw}}, {{C|Calculated Gamble}}, {{C|Concentrate}}, {{C|All-Out Attack}}, {{C|Unload}}, {{C|Storm of Steel}}, {{C|Tools of the Trade}}, {{C|Scrape}}.\n\n====== Relics ======\n{{R|Gambling Chip}}\n\n====== Potions ======\n{{P|Gambler's Brew}}\n\n==== Triggers ====\nThese are everything that triggers on '''Discard''':\n\n====== Cards ======\n{{C|Tactician}}, {{C|Reflex}}, {{C|Eviscerate}}, {{C|Sneaky Strike}}\n\n====== Relics ======\n{{R|Tingsha}}, {{R|Tough Bandages}}, {{R|Hovering Kite}}\n\n=== Orbs ===\n{{Hatnote|See [[Orbs]] for more info.}}\nOrbs are a mechanic used exclusively by the [[Defect]]. Orbs have a passive effect that triggers at the end of your turn. You have a base capacity of 3 Orbs.\n\n==== Channel ====\nChanneling an Orb places it in the right-most empty slot. If an Orb is Channeled when all slots are filled, the rightmost Orb will be Evoked to make room.\n\n==== Evoke ====\nConsume the right-most Orb to trigger a powerful burst effect.\n\n==== Orb Types ====\n* {{KW|Lightning}} Orbs deal 3 (8 when Evoked) damage to a random enemy. {{C|Electrodynamics}} makes Lightning Orbs hit all targets at once.\n* {{KW|Frost}} Orbs give 2 (5 when Evoked) {{KW|Block}}.   (''Frost Orbs have 3 different sprites depending on which slot they are in, only the center sprite is used here.'')\n* {{KW|Dark}} Orbs add 6 damage to its Evoked effect every turn. When Evoked, it will deal that amount of damage to the enemy with the least health.\n* {{KW|Plasma}} Orbs give 1 (2 when Evoked) {{KW|Energy}}. This Orb is not affected by Focus.\n\n==== Focus ====\n{{BD|Focus}} is a buff that increases the effect of Orbs (except for {{KW|Plasma}}). Focus can be negative.\n\n=== Stance ===\nStances are a mechanic used only by the [[Watcher]]. There are 4 Stances (including Neutral/No Stance) each with a significant buff and sometimes a drawback.\n\nSome cards and relics change the [[Watcher]] to other stances. Stances can be exited using the cards {{C|Empty Body}}, {{C|Empty Mind}}, or {{C|Empty Fist}}.\n\n* Neutral/No Stance: [[Watcher]] by default starts with no stance. No bonuses or drawbacks.\n* {{KW|Calm}}: When changing Stances, 2 (3 with {{R|Violet Lotus}}) {{KW|Energy}}.\n* {{KW|Wrath}}: Deal double damage and take double damage. (''Draw 2 Cards'' {{C|Rushdown}})\n* {{KW|Divinity}}: Deal triple damage. Gain 3 {{KW|Energy}}. Exit Divinity at the start of your next turn.\n** Divinity can only be entered by obtaining 10 stacks of {{BD|Mantra}}, using {{C|Blasphemy}}, or using {{P|Ambrosia}}\n\n=== Scry ===\nScry is a mechanic exclusive to the [[Watcher]]. and is defined as this:<blockquote>''Look at the top X cards of your draw pile. You may discard any of them.''</blockquote> \n\nScrying allows you to see a certain amount of cards into your draw pile, allowing you to see what cards are up next and discard them ahead of time.\n\nCards in the Scry screen will always be shown in draw order, with the leftmost card being what you would draw next.\n\nHowever it will not trigger '''Discard''' mechanics, and only functions as deck cycling. Despite the word \"discard\" being used in the description, Scry does not trigger any discard effects.\n\n[[Category:Game Mechanics]]"}}}]},"2014":{"pageid":2014,"ns":0,"title":"Lightning","revisions":[{"revid":55838,"parentid":54199,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Keyword Infobox\n |Name        = Lightning\n |Image       = LightningOrb.png\n |Description = '''Passive''': Deal 3 (+1 per {{BD|Focus}}) damage to a random enemy.<br>{{KW|Evoke}}: Deal 8 (+1 per {{BD|Focus}}) damage to a random enemy.\n}}\n{{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} are the most common damage dealing [[Orb]]. Their [[Orbs#Passive|Passive]] effect deals (3 + {{BD|Focus}}) damage to a random enemy at end of turn. When {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}}, they instead do (8 + {{BD|Focus}}) damage to a random enemy.\n\nLightning is the most common Orb type, having the most cards which Channel it, as well as being generated by both the Defect's starter relic, {{R|Cracked Core}}, and one of its Basics, {{C|Zap}}. It also has the most support of the Orb types, with {{C|Thunder Strike}} scaling based on how many Lightning you've Channeled this combat, as well as {{C|Electrodynamics}} making Lightning Orbs damage all enemies.\n\n== Lightning Sources ==\n=== Cards ===\n* {{C|Zap}}\n* {{C|Ball Lightning}}\n* {{C|Chaos}}\n* {{C|Static Discharge}}\n* {{C|Storm}}\n* {{C|Tempest}}\n* {{C|Electrodynamics}}\n* {{C|Rainbow}}\n=== Relic ===\n* {{R|Cracked Core}}\n\n== Interactions ==\n* Lightning damage bypasses anything that effects {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards, like {{BD|Flying}}, {{BD|Thorns}}, and {{BD|Slow}}.\n* Lightning Orb's [[Orbs#Passive|Passives]] effects happen at end of turn, but before {{KW|Retain}}, so if it kills an enemy and causes {{R|Gremlin Horn}} to draw a card, that card can be Retained.\n* On the other hand, while Lightning ''visually'' happens before end of turn cards such as {{C|Regret}} and {{C|Burn}}, they determine whether they've triggered before Lightning happens. So, if the damage causes {{R|Gremlin Horn}} to draw into one of those cards, that card will ''not'' trigger.\n\n== Synergies ==\n* {{C|Thunder Strike}} hits an additional time for each Lightning Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat.\n* {{C|Electrodynamics}} makes all Lightning Orb [[Orbs#Passive|Passives]] and {{KW|Evoke}} abilities hit ALL enemies.\n* {{C|Bullseye}} applies {{BD|Lock-On}}, which makes damaging Orbs deal 50% more damage to that enemy.\n* {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, and {{P|Potion of Capacity}} all increase your number of Orb Slots, allowing more Orb Passives in parallel.\n* {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, and {{C|Biased Cognition}} all provide {{BD|Focus}}, which increases the damage dealt by Lightning Orbs.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws an additional card for each type of unique Orb Channeled.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Lightning Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n== Anti-Synergies ==\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making Lightning Orbs less effective.\n\n[[Category:Orbs]]"}}}]}}}}